From 5ddab5b8f47fcd9e5b125e3e575d4bbabd6742cf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daan De Meyer <daan.j.demeyer@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 16:15:16 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] portabled: authenticate extension images specified by path

GetImageMetadata() and GetImageMetadataWithExtensions() ask polkit before
inspecting an image that is specified by path, because inspecting
loop-mounts the image as root. Extension images aren't authenticated at
all, so any local user can make portabled set up loop devices for files
they choose, probe them and mount them, by passing them as extensions of
an installed image.

Let's ask polkit for the inspect-images action if any extension image is
specified by path, like we do for the image itself.

Backport note: The NEWS hunk (v263 release notes) and the test hunk
(test/units/TEST-29-PORTABLE.image.sh, introduced with the newer test
harness) were dropped because they do not exist in this 255-based Debian
series. The functional change in src/portable/portabled-image-bus.c
applies as-is.

diff --git a/src/portable/portabled-image-bus.c b/src/portable/portabled-image-bus.c
index 935f0e619b..55e3a3fce0 100644
--- a/src/portable/portabled-image-bus.c
+++ b/src/portable/portabled-image-bus.c
@@ -145,11 +145,20 @@ int bus_image_common_get_metadata(
                 flags |= input_flags;
         }
 
+        /* Inspecting an image loop-mounts it as root, so we authenticate extension images that are
+         * specified by path like the image itself. */
+        bool extension_by_path = false;
+        STRV_FOREACH(i, extension_images)
+                if (!image_name_is_valid(*i)) {
+                        extension_by_path = true;
+                        break;
+                }
+
         r = bus_image_acquire(m,
                               message,
                               name_or_path,
                               image,
-                              BUS_IMAGE_AUTHENTICATE_BY_PATH,
+                              extension_by_path ? BUS_IMAGE_AUTHENTICATE_ALL : BUS_IMAGE_AUTHENTICATE_BY_PATH,
                               "org.freedesktop.portable1.inspect-images",
                               &image,
                               error);
